From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hbadi <badi.hamid@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 17:18:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Build against existing PETSc/SLEPc instead of a fixed
 layout

The cMake/Setup*.cmake modules looked for blas, metis, mumps and slepc
inside ${PETSC_PATH}/arch-linux-c-opt, the layout produced by
install_external_libs/install_petsc.sh and its --download-* flags. Anyone
who installed those libraries from a package manager, or built them
separately, could not configure the project.

Replace them with Find modules that locate an existing installation:
pkg-config first, then the conventional PETSC_DIR / PETSC_ARCH /
SLEPC_DIR variables. Nothing is downloaded or built here.

METIS and MUMPS are no longer required. Neither is included by any source
file, and the HAVE_METIS / HAVE_MUMPS macros they defined are never
tested; both reach the binary through PETSc's own link line. Requiring
them only made configuration fail for no benefit.

Alongside:

- Options for what was hard-coded: BUILD_SHARED_LIBS instead of a forced
  SHARED, SPARSELIZARD_ENABLE_MPI / _GMSH / _OPENMP, and
  _BUILD_EXAMPLES / _BUILD_SIMULATIONS.
- Drop -fPIC -no-pie -O3 and -fopenmp from the compile line; they are
  GCC spellings that no MSVC-style driver accepts. CMAKE_POSITION_-
  INDEPENDENT_CODE, the build type and find_package(OpenMP) do the same
  job portably.
- target_compile_definitions instead of directory-wide add_definitions.
- examples/CMakeLists.txt builds every examples/<name>/main.cpp, staging
  data files per example because their names collide, and registers each
  as a test with its working directory.
- densemat.cpp includes "cblas.h", which oneMKL does not ship; FindCBLAS
  generates a relay header when the vendor header goes by another name.
- universe.cpp called omp_set_num_threads() unguarded, so an OpenMP-less
  build failed to link. It is the only OpenMP call in the project.
- circuit-coupling-rlc-harmonic used std::complex without including
  <complex>, which only worked where another header pulled it in.

Tested on Windows with Intel oneAPI (icx) against a separately built
PETSc 3.25 and SLEPc 3.25: 54 example binaries build and 46 of them run
to completion.

Signed-off-by: hbadi <badi.hamid@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit ea3cc395f96a7da098a02a62b938cf6bcd719d1f)
